 "title": "Simplifying Algebra",
 "summary": "Learn how to turn messy algebra into shorter, cleaner expressions without changing what they mean.",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "In algebra we use letters to represent unknown numbers."
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "When we are writing algebra we do not use a times sign.  \nWe can write a × b as ab  \nWe can write 5 × c as 5c  \nWe can write 6 × a × b as 6ab"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "When we have the same letter multiplied together we can use a power."
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "In the same way that we say the 5 × 5 = 5² we can say that a × a = a²  \nb × b × b = b³  \np × p × p × p × p = p⁵"
  },
  {
   "kind": "mcq-set",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "0aa739ee-9f0b-48d6-9b29-13a03e981072",
     "prompt": "Simplify $c \\times c \\times c \\times c$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$4c$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$c^{4}$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$c^{3}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$4+c$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "There are four factors of $c$ multiplied together, so this is written as $c^{4}$. Adding the $c$ terms would give $4c$, but the operation here is multiplication."
    },
    {
     "id": "17902a44-2af1-46d5-85d1-663ef9e7da48",
     "prompt": "Write $7 \\times m \\times n$ without using a times sign.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$7mn$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$7+m+n$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$mn+7$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$7m+n$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "The number is written first, followed by the letters, so $7 \\times m \\times n$ becomes $7mn$. The multiplication is understood from the notation."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 1: Simplify: 4a × 5b",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "We can multiply the 4 and 5 together  \n4 × 5 = 20\n\nWe now have 20 × a × b  \nWe don't write the times sign in algebra.  \nWe write 20 × a × b as 20ab\n\n**The answer is 20ab**",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "mcq-set",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "a4ba3ecd-6ae9-45b5-a742-2ef24ed087d8",
     "prompt": "Simplify $6p \\times 4q$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$10pq$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$24p+q$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$24pq$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$24p^{2}q^{2}$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Multiply the coefficients: $6 \\times 4=24$. The different letters remain as $pq$, giving $24pq$."
    },
    {
     "id": "9a60793c-8eba-41a3-89a4-d2e62f82d2d0",
     "prompt": "Simplify $4r \\times 3r$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$7r$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$12r$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$12r^{2}$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$7r^{2}$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Multiply the numbers to get $12$, and use $r \\times r=r^{2}$. Therefore the simplified expression is $12r^{2}$."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 2: Simplify: 10t × 3t",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "We can multiply the 10 and 3 together  \n10 × 3 = 30\n\nWe now have 30 × t × t  \nt × t = t²  \n30 × t² = 30t²\n\n**The answer is 30t²**",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "We write division as a fraction  \nWe write a ÷ b as a⁄b"
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 3: Simplify 12a³⁄4a",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "We can look at this question in two parts:  \nWe have 12 ÷ 4  \n12 ÷ 4 = 3  \nWe also have a³ ÷ a  \na³ ÷ a = a²\n\n**The answer is 3a²**",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "mcq-set",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "622eda7b-ff6d-4037-ba06-daf85761135b",
     "prompt": "Simplify $\\frac{15b^{3}}{5b}$.",
